  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Terry Brabant financed part of a historic sailing restoration by selling his Rolls-Royce to pay for a newly cast lead keel. The project depended on retaining a steel hull that had survived decades out of service. His refit used a steel mast and a simple interior, bringing an old racing design back into use on a limited budget.\n\nBrabant chose to keep the boat without an engine, preserving its reliance on sail power. Steve Sleight and Robin Knox-Johnston were involved in the rebuilding work. Once afloat, the restored craft also returned to competition, including occasional appearances in the Round the Island Race.",
